infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Password storage: cost per guess is the whole tradeoff
  desc argon2id makes each guess ~1 billion times more expensive than sha256
  compares
    - label sha256 — wrong for passwords
      children
        - label Cost per guess
          desc ~100 picoseconds
        - label GPU throughput
          desc 10-20 billion guesses/sec on one card
        - label 8-char password
          desc falls in minutes, salted or not
        - label Built for
          desc speed: signatures and integrity checks
    - label argon2id — right for passwords
      children
        - label Cost per guess
          desc ~100 ms tuned (RFC 9106: 64 MiB, 1 pass)
        - label GPU throughput
          desc ~10 guesses/sec — 64 MiB/guess starves it
        - label 8-char password
          desc lifetimes to brute-force
        - label Built for
          desc cost: deliberately expensive per attempt
theme
  palette #f43f5e #10b981
